{#- Written as a template rather than kept in a static folder so the sitemap
    line follows `url` in site_settings.json. A robots.txt that names a sitemap
    on the wrong domain is worse than none: it is the one file a crawler reads
    first, and it would point every one of them somewhere else.

    Nothing is disallowed. The pages that must not be indexed carry their own
    `noindex` meta (the 404 page), and the build report is not published at all:
    it is written to _site_report/, beside the site. -#}
User-agent: *
Allow: /

Sitemap: {{ '/sitemap.xml' | absolute }}
